	"notice": "CC numbers are checked against the manufacturer manual. Connect a MIDI output to the matching input and enable MIDI/CC reception in the device settings. MIDI channel is user-selectable; no USB port-name aliases are assumed. The drawing is a partial grouped control inventory, not a scale panel layout. Touch-key note bindings are virtual defaults and may require octave adjustment. Menu-dependent controls are not automatically bound. NRPN, SysEx preset/sequence transfers, firmware updates and multi-message operations require a protocol-aware application and are not implemented by these static controls. Most sound parameters use 0-99 and portamento 0-31. CC118 is labelled Voice C twice in the printed table; the four-oscillator order and the editor identify it as Voice D coarse tuning. Voice count and effects can vary with firmware; this profile does not assume the updated firmware.",
